    "analysis_type": "paradigm_network",
    "rationale": "Several symbols support true compositional paradigms with stable substitution frames: C+/C-, Eo/E-/E~, Fo/F-/F+/Ff, H!/H?/Hw/H-/H0/Hq/Hr/Hz, T+/T-, Pm/Ps/Pf/Palt, and K/K+/ok+/wrong+. Other lookalikes such as C-dark, E-fade, F-ok, F-rim-, H-thin, Hth, and Hol do not participate in a coherent multi-entry paradigm with predictable part meanings, so they remain lexical. Homographic standalone symbols like C, F, T, and K are left lexical while the same surface strings are used as morphemes inside supported constructions.",
